UNIT get_rgb
LANG js
PRIMARY-SHA256 b0378dc3a8ba5eb040db7f4ad96183c769e6a688cb76770da16da9ab5a6f6d65
SIG get_rgb(input: string): [number, number, number, number] | null
NOTE default export
ABI text=string (UTF-16); num=number (f64); tuple=Array; none=null. "Empty text" (R1) is the falsy string "".
  The real package is driven as default.get.rgb(input); the reconstruction exports a plain function.
MECHANISM RE flavor ECMAScript with the i flag; "whole text" (R2) = ^ and $ anchors; "lowercased" (R8) =
  String.prototype.toLowerCase; "round halves toward +infinity" (R6) = Math.round; word characters (R8) = \w.
MECHANISM numeric parse (R5, R6) = parseFloat on the captured text; hex byte (R3, R4) = parseInt(pair, 16).
CARRIED colorNames = ../carried-color-names.js (default export: a plain object; membership (R8) = own-property lookup)
DEPENDS-ON none
PINNED regex HEX6    = /^#([a-f\d]{6})([a-f\d]{2})?$/i CITED R3 — the accept-set rides on it
PINNED regex ABBR    = /^#([a-f\d]{3,4})$/i CITED R4
PINNED regex NUMERIC = /^rgba?\(\s*([+-]?(?:\d*\.)?\d+(?:e\d+)?)(?=[\s,])\s*(?:,\s*)?([+-]?(?:\d*\.)?\d+(?:e\d+)?)(?=[\s,])\s*(?:,\s*)?([+-]?(?:\d*\.)?\d+(?:e\d+)?)\s*(?:[\s,|/]\s*([+-]?(?:\d*\.)?\d+(?:e\d+)?)(%?)\s*)?\)$/i CITED R5 — the (?=[\s,]) lookaheads after channels 1 and 2 ARE the "must be followed by whitespace or comma" rule; EARNED the transcription-register SIR established these lookaheads as load-bearing (percent-channel and 2-channel rejects)
PINNED regex PERCENT = /^rgba?\(\s*([+-]?[\d.]+)%\s*,?\s*([+-]?[\d.]+)%\s*,?\s*([+-]?[\d.]+)%\s*(?:[\s,|/]\s*([+-]?[\d.]+)(%?)\s*)?\)$/i CITED R6
PINNED regex KEYWORD = /^(\w+)$/ CITED R8 — applied to the lowercased text
PROVENANCE verified JS reconstruction: sir-lab/color-string-rederive/runs/emit_1.mjs (3/3 blind quorum;
  5000/5000 differential vs index.corrected.js). This file was split out of the transcription-register SIR 2026-09-22.
